BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:khn-center-residency-fall-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: KHN Center for the Arts: Artist Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Kimmel Harding Nelson Center for the Arts (KHN) in Nebraska
  City supports established and emerging writers\, visual artists\, and com
 posers/musicians by providing living and studio space that allows uninterr
 upted time for work\, reflection\, and creative growth. Residencies run 2 
 to 8 weeks and include free living and studio space plus a USD 175/week st
 ipend. KHN awards approximately 30-38 residencies per session\, of which r
 oughly 8-12 go to visual artists working in various media. Categories: Wri
 ters & Poets\, Visual Artists\, Composers & Musicians\, and Interdisciplin
 ary Artists. Visual artists work in one of three studios (two approximatel
 y 425 sq ft and one 258 sq ft) outfitted with work tables\, running water\
 , and storage shelves\; donated hand tools\, a bandsaw\, miter saw\, and p
 ainting easels are available. Upon request\, artists with previous printin
 g experience may access the onsite Harry Duncan Letterpress Studio (SP15 V
 andercook Proof Press\, a 16x12 inch boxcar base for adhesive plates\, fur
 niture\, fonts\, and a small inventory of printmaking tools). Open interna
 tionally. Applications are reviewed twice a year (deadlines 1 March and 1 
 September)\; the 2027 1st Session (deadline 1 September 2026) is for award
 s scheduled 4 January to 25 June 2027. All applications must be submitted 
 online via SlideRoom\; mailed or emailed applications are not considered. 
 A $35 application fee is collected through the portal.\n\nOrganisation: Ki
 mmel Harding Nelson Center for the Arts\nLocation: Nebraska City\, Nebrask
 a\, United States. Open internationally.\nAward: USD 175/week stipend\, pl
 us free living and studio space. $35 application fee\, collected via the S
 lideRoom application portal.\nDuration: Residencies of 2-8 weeks\; applica
 tions reviewed in two annual cycles (1 March and 1 September). The 2027 1s
 t Session covers awards scheduled 4 January to 25 June 2027.\n\nMore: http
 s://www.khncenterforthearts.org/residencyresident-application/how-apply?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.khncenterforthearts.org/residencyresident-application/how-a
 pply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nebraska City\, Nebraska\, United States. Open internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:npaf-hawaii-volcanoes-residency-october-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261010T121220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Deadline: National Parks Arts Foundation: Hawai'i Volcanoes Nationa
 l Park Residency\, October 2027 (All Media)
DESCRIPTION:The National Parks Arts Foundation offers a one-month\, all-med
 ia residency in Hawai'i Volcanoes National Park on the Big Island\, a UNES
 CO World Heritage Site spanning the Kilauea and Mauna Loa volcanoes\, for 
 October 2027. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 4\,000 stipend\, housing in a spacious t
 wo-story three-bedroom house just outside the park boundaries (with record
 ing booth\, meditation area and art-studio conversion with ocean views\, c
 lose to beaches and about 30 minutes by car from park headquarters)\, stud
 io space\, artist events and publicity. Residents give a public event or p
 resentation\, and donating an artwork to the NPS collections is considered
  but not required. ELIGIBILITY: open to all artists\, writers\, musicians 
 and performance artists\; single artists\, couples\, families and groups o
 f 3 or more may apply. COSTS: application fee of USD 60 (single)\, USD 120
  (couple/duo) or USD 160 (group of 3+)\; artists cover their own transport
 ation and required insurance. Note that NPAF does not refund fees if the p
 rogram is interrupted or cancelled by natural events (volcanic hazards\, w
 eather) or government shutdowns. Apply via Submittable. NOTIFICATION: 16 N
 ovember 2026. DEADLINE: 20 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: National Parks A
 rts Foundation (NPAF)\nLocation: Hawai'i Volcanoes National Park\, Big Isl
 and\, Hawaii\, US. Open to all artists\, writers\, musicians and performan
 ce artists\; single artists\, couples\, families and groups may apply.\nAw
 ard: USD 4\,000 stipend\, plus a month's housing in a three-bedroom house 
 with recording booth\, meditation area and art-studio conversion\, about 3
 0 minutes from park headquarters. Travel and required insurance are the ar
 tist's own responsibility. APPLICATION FEE: USD 60 single artist\, USD 120
  couple or duo\, USD 160 group of 3 or more.\nDuration: One month\, 6 to 3
 1 October 2027.\n\nMore: https://nationalparksartsfoundation.submittable.c
 om/submit/367795/hawaii-volcanoes-national-park-october-2027-all-artistic-
 media-genres-residenc?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://nationalparksartsfoundation.submittable.com/submit/367795/hawai
 i-volcanoes-national-park-october-2027-all-artistic-media-genres-residenc?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hawai'i Volcanoes National Park\, Big Island\, Hawaii\, US. Open t
 o all artists\, writers\, musicians and performance artists\; single artis
 ts\, couples\, families and groups may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wave-farm-research-production-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Wave Farm: 2027 Research and Production Program (Transmis
 sion Art Residencies and Radio Art Fellowships\, NY)
DESCRIPTION:Wave Farm\, the Warhol Foundation-backed transmission arts cent
 er in Acra\, NY\, opens one application covering all its 2027 opportunitie
 s: the Transmission Art Residency\, the Spatial Sound Residency\, and two 
 Radio Art Fellowship tracks (Research\, and Community Engagement) connecte
 d to Wave Farm's WGXC radio station. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 1\,000 stipend fo
 r each 10-day residency and USD 2\,000 for each two-month fellowship\, wit
 h access to Wave Farm's research library\, transmitter and receiver equipm
 ent\, and on-site staff support to develop a new transmission artwork. ELI
 GIBILITY: international\; collaborations allowed\; full-time students are 
 ineligible except rare post-graduate cases\; past residents and fellows ma
 y reapply\; applicants may apply to as many opportunities as they wish but
  will be offered at most one\; DJ sets are explicitly ineligible. A strong
  fit for signal-based\, broadcast\, spatial sound and radio-adjacent work.
  DEADLINE: 1 December 2026 at 11:59 pm EST. Finalists are interviewed by Z
 oom\, with notifications in late February 2027 and residencies during 2027
 .\n\nOrganisation: Wave Farm\nLocation: Wave Farm\, Acra\, NY\, US (Catski
 ll Mountain Park). International open call.\nAward: USD 1\,000 stipend for
  each 10-day residency\; USD 2\,000 for each two-month Radio Art Fellowshi
 p. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 days (Transmission Art and Spatial So
 und residencies) or 2 months (Radio Art Fellowships)\, during 2027.\n\nMor
 e: https://wavefarm.org/ta/residency-program/info-apply?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wavefarm.org/ta/residency-program/info-apply?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wave Farm\, Acra\, NY\, US (Catskill Mountain Park). International
  open call.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eyebeam-agency-virtual-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eyebeam AGENCY Virtual Residency\, Fall 2026 (US-based ar
 tists)
DESCRIPTION:Eyebeam's 2026-27 program year runs under the theme AGENCY: pre
 serving human agency as AI systems increasingly act\, decide and carry out
  tasks on our behalf\, asserting agency in imagining and building the soci
 eties we inhabit\, and rethinking agency as collective\, relational\, enta
 ngled and more-than-human. The Virtual Residency (Fall/Winter) supports US
 -based artists working outside New York City with time\, community and str
 ucture to develop new work around the theme\; it is well-suited to early-s
 tage projects where shared research\, discussion groups and feedback on na
 scent ideas would advance concept development and prototyping. Projects mi
 ght engage AI directly but do not have to\; Eyebeam welcomes critical and 
 creative approaches to power\, autonomy\, technological systems\, collecti
 ve action\, human and nonhuman relationships\, and the structures through 
 which agency is exercised\, including reimagining AI systems through colle
 ctive governance\, repair\, rehearsal or mischief\, and repurposing AI tow
 ard tools for the public good. STRUCTURE: six artists\, 12 weeks\, minimum
  3-4 hours per week\, with weekly cohort sessions\, independent project de
 velopment\, work-in-progress shares with peers and guest critics\, a closi
 ng virtual process presentation\, and a contribution to an end-of-year pub
 lication. ELIGIBILITY: individuals only (no collectives this cycle)\; not 
 enrolled in a full-time degree program\; not committed to another residenc
 y during the term\; US-based outside NYC for the full term. TIMELINE: dead
 line Sunday 11 October 2026\, 11:59 PM ET (no late applications)\; intervi
 ews 26-28 October\; notifications 29 October\; residency 4 November 2026 t
 o 12 February 2027. Info session Monday 28 September 2026\, 1 PM ET. Apply
  via Submittable\, free.\n\nOrganisation: Eyebeam\nLocation: Online. Appli
 cants must be based in the United States\, OUTSIDE New York City\, and rem
 ain US-based for the full residency term (4 November 2026 to 12 February 2
 027).\nAward: USD 2\,000 stipend for each of six selected artists\, plus w
 eekly residency programming\, mentorship with Eyebeam alumni and visiting 
 professionals\, technical consultation\, and access to tools and expertise
  through Eyebeam's network. No application fee (via Submittable).\nDuratio
 n: 12 weeks\, 4 November 2026 to 12 February 2027\; minimum commitment 3-4
  hours per week.\n\nMore: https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-virtual-resi
 dency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-virtual-residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online. Applicants must be based in the United States\, OUTSIDE Ne
 w York City\, and remain US-based for the full residency term (4 November 
 2026 to 12 February 2027).
END:VEVENT
