SUMMARY:Deadline: LA Department of Cultural Affairs: NEAR + CO-UP Artist Re
 sidency Grants 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The City of Los Angeles' residency-based grant line for sociall
 y engaged art. Neighborhood Engagement Artist Residencies (NEAR\, USD 12\,
 000) fund individual teaching-artists to run participatory\, multi-session
  residency projects in self-selected non-arts venues (community organizati
 ons\, civic spaces) across LA's Council Districts\, reaching audiences wit
 h little exposure to arts programming. Creative Optimism-Uplifting Promise
 s (CO-UP\, USD 15\,000) funds collaborations between social-justice nonpro
 fits and artists for community-driven arts projects and public events. Bot
 h lines run on one autumn application cycle for the 2027-28 framework. ELI
 GIBILITY: Los Angeles-based artists and host or partner organizations\; pr
 ojects must take place in the City of Los Angeles. DEADLINE: 30 October 20
 26\, 11:59 PM via the DCA grants portal.\n\nOrganisation: City of Los Ange
 les Department of Cultural Affairs (DCA)\nLocation: Los Angeles\, US. Resi
 dencies take place in non-arts venues across the City of Los Angeles\; for
  LA-based artists and partner organizations.\nAward: NEAR grants of USD 12
 \,000 for individual artists\; CO-UP grants of USD 15\,000 for collaborati
 ons between social-justice nonprofits and artists. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Multi-session residencies during the 2027-28 cycle\n\nMore: https:
 //culture.lacity.gov/grants/near-co-op?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.lacity.gov/grants/near-co-op?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Los Angeles\, US. Residencies take place in non-arts venues across
  the City of Los Angeles\; for LA-based artists and partner organizations.
END:VEVENT
