DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Deadline: Adirondack Experience (ADKX) Artist-in-Residence 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Adirondack Experience museum on Blue Mountain Lake offers f
 our one-month artist residencies for June\, July\, August and September 20
 27. Residents work publicly on their own practice a minimum of six hours a
  day (roughly 10:00-16:00) three days a week in the museum's public areas\
 , and spend two days a week (Fridays and Saturdays\, 10:00-16:30) engaging
  visitors in the Art Lab makerspace. WHAT YOU GET: USD 5\,000 stipend for 
 the residency\, USD 500 travel allowance\, USD 250 Art Lab materials allow
 ance\, and free housing in a large bedroom on the second floor of the muse
 um's Residence building with shared bathroom\, kitchen and dining access\,
  parking\, utilities\, wi-fi and laundry. ELIGIBILITY: visual artists with
  a portfolio of at least five works exhibited publicly (museums\, public\,
  university or private galleries) or sold to private collectors\; digital 
 and performance artists must explain how visitors will have an enriching e
 xperience watching them at work\; open internationally\, but ADKX cannot s
 ponsor visas\, so non-US artists arrange their own. CONDITIONS: artists pr
 ovide their own materials outside the Art Lab allowance\, and the museum r
 etains first option to purchase one work created during the residency at f
 air market price. APPLICATION: email the completed application package to 
 cbraunstein@theadkx.org. DEADLINE: 11 December 2026\, 17:00 EST.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Adirondack Experience\, The Museum on Blue Mountain Lake (ADKX)\nL
 ocation: Blue Mountain Lake\, New York\, USA. Open internationally\; non-U
 S artists arrange their own visas.\nAward: USD 5\,000 stipend per one-mont
 h residency\, plus USD 500 travel allowance\, USD 250 Art Lab materials al
 lowance\, and free on-site housing with utilities\, wi-fi and laundry incl
 uded.\nDuration: One month: June\, July\, August or September 2027 (four r
 esidencies awarded).\n\nMore: https://www.theadkx.org/adirondack-experienc
 e-artist-in-residence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.theadkx.org/adirondack-experience-artist-in-residence/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Blue Mountain Lake\, New York\, USA. Open internationally\; non-US
  artists arrange their own visas.
END:VEVENT
